Title: SECOND COAST
Author: Emily Nakamura
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. CAPE COD INN - ESTABLISHING - DAWN

Weathered shingles. Quiet Atlantic. A retreat week begins.

EXT. CAPE COD INN - PORCH - DAWN

CLAIRE HART watches a taxi arrive. JAMES MERCER steps out with a LEATHER SATCHEL.
CLAIRE
You said you'd never come back east.

INT. INN LOBBY - MORNING

Adjacent room keys. Awkward reach. The innkeeper pretends not to notice.
CLAIRE
I'm here to work. Not to time-travel.

INT. RETREAT WORKSHOP - DAY

Twelve writers around a table. Claire reads a passage. James listens, still.
WORKSHOP LEADER
Strong voice. Who's the 'you' in this scene?
CLAIRE
Someone I used to know. Present tense optional.

EXT. BEACH - AFTERNOON

James produces the old PHOTO. Wind tries to take it.
JAMES
We looked happy. I forgot we were.

INT. INN DINING ROOM - NIGHT

Retreat dinner. Claire sits with a poet from Vermont. James watches from the bar.
JAMES
Buy you a drink for old times' sake?
CLAIRE
Old times owe me interest.

INT. CLAIRE'S ROOM - NIGHT

Tea through the connecting door. Rain on the windows.
CLAIRE
Why now? Why this week?
JAMES
Because your new book mentions a lighthouse I've never forgotten.

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE PATH - MORNING

They walk in silence. The LEATHER SATCHEL swings at James's side.
CLAIRE
You dedicated it to me before you told me goodbye.

INT. JAMES'S ROOM - AFTERNOON

Claire reads his manuscript — a love story that stops at page ninety.
CLAIRE
You left the ending blank.
JAMES
I didn't know if you'd give me one.

EXT. BEACH - SUNSET

Dunes, gold light. Claire closes the satchel — keeps the manuscript, not the photo.
CLAIRE
One chapter at a time. No promises past this week.
JAMES
I'll take one chapter. I've waited eight years for a page turn.

FADE OUT.


THE END
